PATCH 490: the saved-game / file-list pick dialog cbd4 wrote an UNINITIALISED value into the engine's PIT
tick counter -- the twin defect patch 143 fixed in cb74.

asm 0xcbd4-0xcc32 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): `push [0x452]` saves the click timestamp across the dialog and both
exits `pop [0x452]` it back.  Ghidra invented `DAT_1000_c452 = unaff_CS` instead, so the tick counter was
overwritten with whatever the compiler left in that slot -- different at -O0 (native) and -O2 (wasm).
The rest of the function was base-lost as well: the picked entry's 13-byte name is copied out of the
STRSEG (ES = word[DGROUP:0x70]) at word[0xe838]*0x10+0x3776 into the caller's buffer word[0xe855], and the
result is the entry word at STRSEG:0x3f76+idx*2, with CF=1 on cancel.  Found because it left different
scratch at DGROUP:0xe855 on the two targets, which showed up the moment the cross-target fingerprint was
widened to the full roster region (0x9000..0xefff).
